From 99f8cda2b090a25d58320605c46759a43f0fe123 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naresh Solanki <naresh.solanki.2011@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:31:12 +0530
Subject: net: dsa: mt7530: support the mtk-8021q tagger

Implement change_tag_protocol and the tag_8021q VLAN callbacks so an
MT7530 can run with 802.1Q tags on its CPU port, selected with
dsa-tag-protocol = "mtk-8021q" or at runtime through the conduit's
dsa/tagging attribute.

In this mode every user port and the CPU port forward by VLAN table
(security mode). Each tag_8021q VLAN is its user port's PVID, egress-
untagged there and egress-tagged towards the CPU; bridge join/leave go
through dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_join/leave. Only VLAN-unaware bridging is
supported: VLAN filtering is refused and bridge VLAN ops are no-ops.

Unlike MTK-tagged frames, which carry an explicit destination bitmap,
802.1Q frames from the CPU are subject to the CPU port's own setup, so:
- PVC[31:16] holds the TPID (0x8100) the port matches tags against;
  the MTK-tag setup leaves it 0 and every CPU frame was dropped
- the CPU port's cached port matrix (ports[].pm) is kept at all user
  ports: port_enable() rewrites the matrix from it, and the MTK-tag
  setup never fills it in for the CPU port (matrix 0, all dropped)
- the CPU port forwards in FID_BRIDGED's STP state

Signed-off-by: Naresh Solanki <naresh.solanki.2011@gmail.com>
